From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Lawler <patricktlawler@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 17:20:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: use the BE550 IPQ9574 support

Replace the IPQ9574 support from the previous patches with the version
tested on the TP-Link Archer BE550. Compared to them, it:

- sets get_ring_selector in ipq9574_ops: ath11k_dp_tx() calls it for
  every data frame, so without it the first frame to a client
  dereferences a NULL pointer
- disables cold boot calibration: with it, the Q6 reports a fatal
  error when the host sends the mission mode request after the
  calibration, and the remoteproc does not recover
- drops max_tx_ring, which ath11k_hw_params no longer has
- reuses the IPQ8074 CE configuration and the IPQ6018 service map
  instead of IPQ9574 copies (the service map copy is identical, the
  host CE copy is the IPQ8074 one without CE10 and CE11)
- does not advertise the PCIe PME D3cold host capability for the AHB
  IPQ9574 radio, as in Igor Kravchenko's Xiaomi BE7000 work
- adds IPQ9574 last in enum ath11k_hw_rev, the OF match table, the
  probe switch and ath11k_hw_params[], named "ipq9574 hw1.0" like the
  other entries, with cbcal_restart_fw set as for IPQ8074 and IPQ6018
- drops the unused ATH11K_QMI_IPQ9574_M3_DUMP_ADDRESS and the extra
  warning when handling firmware ready fails

Signed-off-by: Patrick Lawler <patricktlawler@gmail.com>
